==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|fec}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*faką||division, piece, part}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*pāǵe-||to nail, fasten}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|fek|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon [[fak]] (Dutch [[vak]]), Old High German [[fah]] (German [[Fach]]), Latin [[pangere]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fæk/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n|facu}}

# a [[division]], [[space]]
# a portion, period, or space of time; while; an [[interval]]
# period of five years, [[lustrum]]

